      "summaries": {
        "en": "Grok-1 is an open-source large language model developed by xAI that provides researchers and developers with transparent access to advanced AI capabilities for experimentation and innovation. Its architecture features a unique mixture-of-experts design with 314 billion parameters, enabling efficient scaling and specialized task handling through selective activation of neural pathways. Developers can fine-tune the model on custom datasets using the provided Python codebase, implement it for creative text generation, or study its reasoning mechanisms to advance natural language understanding research.",
        "zh": "Grok-1是由xAI开发的开源大型语言模型，为研究者和开发者提供了透明访问先进AI能力的机会，支持实验与创新。该模型采用独特的混合专家架构，包含3140亿参数，通过选择性激活神经通路实现高效扩展和专业化任务处理。用户可利用Python代码库在自定义数据集上微调模型，应用于创意文本生成，或研究其推理机制以推进自然语言理解领域的发展。这种设计让开发者能够探索大规模模型的内部工作机制，并基于实际需求构建定制化AI应用。",
        "es": "Grok-1 is an open-source large language model developed by xAI that provides researchers and developers with transparent access to advanced AI capabilities for experimentation and innovation. Its architecture features a unique mixture-of-experts design with 314 billion parameters, enabling efficient scaling and specialized task handling through selective activation of neural pathways. Developers can fine-tune the model on custom datasets using the provided Python codebase, implement it for creative text generation, or study its reasoning mechanisms to advance natural language understanding research.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "grok-1 gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Grok-1 is an open-source large language model developed by xAI that provides researchers and developers with transparent access to advanced AI capabilities for experimentation and innovation. Its architecture features a unique mixture-of-experts design with 314 billion parameters, enabling efficient scaling and specialized task handling through selective activation of neural pathways. Developers can fine-tune the model on custom datasets using the provided Python codebase, implement it for creative text generation, or study its reasoning mechanisms to advance natural language understanding research.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/xai-org/grok-1 for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
