          "what": "Data-Science-For-Beginners is a comprehensive 10-week curriculum that makes data science accessible to newcomers by breaking down complex concepts into 20 manageable lessons. It teaches practical skills through hands-on Jupyter Notebook exercises, emphasizing real-world applications with Python libraries like pandas for data analysis and visualization. Learners can follow the structured weekly modules to build foundational knowledge, then apply these techniques to their own datasets or explore more advanced topics in the field.",
